HANDOFF / CLAIM RELEASED
Session: ADB991-claude-20261116-3be0
Claim: https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/issues/478#issuecomment-6932290219

PR: https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/pull/480 (draft). The report is `blueprint/units/YM-000026/reviews/relativistic-reconstruction-math-review-ADB991-claude-20261116-3be0.md`; the reviewed files are those of `main` 962ac43b, with per-file hashes in the report.

**Established.** All eleven files of the *Relativistic reconstruction* section were read line by line, and signs, conventions and quantifiers were recomputed. No error was found in the section's own proofs. This includes:
- the complex heat extension and the sign `V(t)=e^{itH}`;
- the joint boundary edge-Taylor formula;
- the Fourier and cone support;
- the boost Ward identity;
- the full tube with its cutoff margins and covariance;
- the mixed heat Gram identity;
- the word construction;
- boundary detection;
- the SNAG/Paley positive-energy argument;
- the imaginary-boost locality argument, including germ equality on the Euclidean slice and the passage from germs to boundary distributions.

**Findings needing an author.**
- **F1:** the reference Lorentz action `T_d^0` required by `input:calibrated-actions` is not constructed anywhere in the monograph. The input requires a boost generator `-iL^0`, agreement with `R_d^0` on spatial rotations, and commutation with `J_d^0`. `physical-angular-actions.tex` treats this action as fixed. Lean proves it as `YM.Maxwell.Free.voyage` / `launched` (`Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/Descent.lean:173-181`).
- **F2:** the identification of involutions assumed in `cor:word-motion-inputs` is not discharged by name in `assembly.tex`.
- **E1-E4:** editorial items, listed in the report.

**Uncertain or unchecked.**
- The literature locators were not re-read against the originals (the proxy returned 403); the report relies on the #472 record.
- The upstream inputs to this section were not re-proved.
- Lean correspondence was not checked.

**Next.** A manuscript author adds the free Lorentz companion subsection (F1) and the assembly sentence (F2). An independent human reviewer is still needed for acceptance under #26.

Prepared autonomously by Claude (Anthropic) running as a scheduled agent on behalf of @ADB991; ADB991 had not reviewed it before submission.
